From 2c96fdcdfd82387fcd62abafa2c933e1ea84d873 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 19:20:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] linker: fix 9 correctness bugs found by new differential
 test suite

New tests/linker/run_linker_tests.py: 64 differential regression tests
using GNU ld (bfd), mold 2.37 and wild 0.10 as oracles. Fixes:

1. COMMON vs strong definition: strong def in a later object now
   supersedes a tentative (SHN_COMMON) definition; largest COMMON wins
   among tentative defs (GNU semantics).
2. Duplicate strong definitions are now a hard 'multiple definition'
   error instead of silently keeping the first.
3. .init_array/.fini_array/.ctors/.dtors inputs are sorted by numeric
   priority suffix (SORT_BY_INIT_PRIORITY), fixing
   __attribute__((constructor(P))) ordering.
4. --gc-sections keeps SHF_GNU_RETAIN sections and sections referenced
   via __start_/__stop_ bracket symbols; -e/-u symbols are GC roots.
5. IFUNC in dynamic executables: IRELATIVE entries are now emitted into
   .rela.dyn (previously calls bound to the *resolver*, silently
   returning the implementation pointer as result).
6. .preinit_array: mapped, laid out, DT_PREINIT_ARRAY/SZ emitted.
7. GOTTPOFF IE->LE relaxation transplants REX.R into REX.B and supports
   add (0x03) as well as mov (0x8b); previously %r12 became %rsp,
   corrupting the stack in static-TLS pthread programs.
8. -Wl,-e/--entry=SYM honored for the ELF entry point.
9. --wrap=SYM and -u/--undefined=SYM implemented (symbol-table rewrite
   + forced-undefined archive extraction).
