Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 19:43:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] linker: implement TLS General-Dynamic / Local-Dynamic
 models (x86-64)

Previously any object compiled with -fpic that touched an extern
__thread variable failed to link ('unsupported relocation type 19').

Executables (emit_exec):
* R_X86_64_TLSGD: GD->LE relaxation for locally-bound symbols
  (mov %fs:0,%rax; lea tpoff(%rax),%rax), GD->IE for dynamic TLS
  symbols via a GOT slot carrying R_X86_64_TPOFF64.
* R_X86_64_TLSLD: LD->LE relaxation to the canonical 12-byte
  mov %fs:0,%rax sequence; subsequent DTPOFF32/64 become TP-relative.
* TLSDESC (GOTPC32_TLSDESC + TLSDESC_CALL) -> LE relaxation.
* The consumed __tls_get_addr call relocation is suppressed via
  byte-range tracking instead of fragile instruction matching.

Shared libraries (emit_shared):
* True GD: (DTPMOD64, DTPOFF64) GOT pairs per TLSGD symbol; DTPOFF
  resolved statically for local definitions, dynamically for
  interposable ones.
* True LD: single (DTPMOD64, 0) GOT pair; DTPOFF32 applied statically.

5 new differential tests (GD, LD, GD-across-.so, LD-in-dlopen'd-.so,
mixed IE/GD/LE) all matching bfd/mold/wild behavior.
