From 0d1999208b5b3189f3c7bf1aaac8533c2dfa047d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 19:50:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] linker: eliminate O(n^2) hot paths; add link-speed
 benchmark harness

Root cause analysis on a 12k-GOT-symbol stress link (120 objects,
-fpic): 216 ms vs 53 ms for GNU bfd. Culprits, all quadratic:
* Vec::contains dedup scans in create_plt_got / plt+GOT collection
* dyn_sym_names.iter().position() per dynamic relocation entry
* got_entries[..gi] prefix counting per applied GOT relocation

Fixes: ordered Vec + FxHashSet shadow sets for dedup, an O(1)
name->dynsym-index FxHashMap built after the .gnu.hash bucket sort,
and a precomputed GOT slot ordinal table.

Result on the same stress case: 216 ms -> 49 ms (4.4x), now at parity
with bfd and ahead of mold. tests/linker/bench_linker.py (new) shows
lccc ahead of bfd AND mold on all synthetic profiles:
  medium (151 objs): lccc 25 ms, bfd 44 ms, mold 52 ms
  large  (401 objs): lccc 60 ms, bfd 115 ms, mold 103 ms
  large --gc-sections: lccc 49 ms, bfd 131 ms, mold 96 ms
All 69 differential linker tests + 147 compiler regressions still pass.
