MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New linker_common/linker_script.rs: complete parser + expression evaluator
for the GNU ld script language subset the kernel needs — ENTRY, PHDRS with
FLAGS, SECTIONS with location-counter arithmetic, in-section symbol
assignments, PROVIDE, ALIGN/ABSOLUTE/ADDR/LOADADDR/SIZEOF/DEFINED/MIN/MAX,
ASSERT, AT() load addresses, KEEP/SORT/SORT_BY_ALIGNMENT input specs,
/DISCARD/, fill patterns (=0xcccccccc), :phdr assignment, numeric K/M
suffixes, CONSTANT(MAXPAGESIZE), and glob patterns incl. char classes
([0-9a-zA-Z_]). Unit tests cover a kernel-shaped script.

New x86/linker/emit_script.rs: script-driven layout engine — first-match-wins
input assignment in script order, forward/deferred symbol assignment to a
fixed point, per-section LMA (AT), PHDR spanning with p_paddr, LMA-congruent
file offsets at 2 MiB pages, GNU-compatible symbol attribution for
end-of-section symbols (_end in .brk), empty-output-section suppression
(objcopy compatibility), full .symtab for System.map/kallsyms flows.

New src/bin/lccc-ld: GNU-ld-compatible CLI (-m/-z/-T/--script/--whole-archive/
--start-group/-Map/--strip-*, --build-id/--orphan-handling accepted) with
whole-command-line group loading incl. thin archives (vmlinux.a).

PROOF: make LD=lccc-ld bzImage on Linux 6.18.44 tinyconfig+serial links
vmlinux via lccc-ld with layout matching GNU ld (all key symbols SAME:
init_stack, _text, _etext, __bss_*, __brk_*, _end, per-cpu, jiffies,
startup_64, phys_startup_64) and the resulting bzImage BOOTS IN QEMU all
the way into userspace (busybox init prints uname from the running kernel).
